WEBVTT

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.510
<i>Second bout. On the east side, Tsuji-kun.</i>

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:06.730
<i>On the west side, Sawai-kun.</i>

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.690
Huh? Who's that?

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.240
He was sitting where
the trainer usually sits.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.090
So he's a sumo wrestler, too?

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.660
Dachi High, fight!

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.080
I'm sorry, Coach.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.670
I tried a move we hadn't
discussed beforehand.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.150
And this was the result.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.210
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.670
You did what I asked and then some.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.680
The fact that you still lost...

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.290
is a failure on my part.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:48.400
I couldn't keep the promise I made to you
about getting you a win at Nationals.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.440
I'm truly sorry.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.450
Please don't apologize.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.810
Without you, I wouldn't even
have forced the tie.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:01.950
I have no regrets.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.960
I was able to go in all guns blazing,

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:09.960
because Dachi High has the 
strongest reserve member ever.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.050
Dachi High's fate is in your hands, Coach.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.220
I mean...

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.860
Kirihito.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:57.030
<b>Bout 22
"The Forgotten National Treasure, Onikiri Yasutsuna"</b>

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.360
Sumo wrestlers have to be large and heavy.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.370
Onimaru and Kariya are
exceptions to the rule.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.120
Just 'cause there are no weight categories
doesn't mean anyone can do it.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.310
So which camp do you fall into?

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.080
Are you an "exception to the rule"
that can take on a super-heavyweight?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:13.690
Or are you—

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:14.480
Hey.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:19.190
I'm soaking in the atmosphere of my 
first official bout in a very long time.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:22.210
Think you could stop flapping your gums?

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.410
He's better at trash-talk than Sawai.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.620
Aw, but Leon-chan's such a nice person.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.230
He should drop the bad guy act.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.730
<i>I didn't expect to see him in the ring.</i>

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.940
<i>He showed no indication of taking the ring
when he came to our school.</i>

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.840
<i>I wonder why they look so relaxed.</i>

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.810
<i>Is Tsuji strong?</i>

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.830
<i>If he is, why did they keep
putting Mitsuhashi in?</i>

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.580
<i>It's fine. Tsuji will come through for us.</i>

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.130
<i>Even though he can only fight for 20 seconds,</i>

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.670
<i>he's managed to throw both
Ushio and Master Shibakiyama.</i>

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.740
<i>In those 20 seconds,
he's the strongest sumo around.</i>

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.650
<i>I've managed to remain out of the limelight</i>

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.390
<i>because Mitsuhashi
managed to cling on till now.</i>

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:17.010
<i>And if he hadn't encouraged me,</i>

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.040
<i>I would've given up on ever
standing in the ring again.</i>

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:25.030
<i>I won't waste this chance you've given me!</i>

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.270
Hands on the ground!

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.080
<i>This guy...</i>

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.260
<i>He seemed like a smug dick at first glance,</i>

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.490
<i>but that look in his eyes
is seriously intense.</i>

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:41.680
Right, let's see Onikiri in action.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:50.310
Spirit!

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.810
<i>He charged head-first at
a much bigger opponent?!</i>

00:04:58.850 --> 00:04:59.650
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.900
<i>This guy...</i>

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.990
<i>Sorry, I don't have time to mess about.</i>

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.450
<i>I'm going to end this now!</i>

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.690
Push, Kirihito!

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:14.750
No...

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.670
His grip's been altered.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.250
He can't push effectively!

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:20.380
<i>I'm wasting time!</i>

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.090
<i>Try this on for size!</i>

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.050
<i>He's not an Eiga High regular for nothing!</i>

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.370
<i>He's strong!</i>

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.480
<i>His techniques are top notch.</i>

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.520
<i>If he catches me off-guard, I'm done for!</i>

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.120
I don't get it.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.940
Why is this guy only a reserve?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.590
Maybe he's injured or something.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.530
<i>He does seem to be rushing for some reason.</i>

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.890
<i>In any case, I can't let him
 grab the initiative.</i>

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.140
It's not looking good.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:57.510
Sawai is smarter than he looks.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.230
The professor's at his best
when he's countering moves.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.660
He struggles if his opponent
waits for him to come at them.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.960
Just budging an opponent that size

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.740
will take more strength
than Coach can muster.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.590
<i>If I stand still, I'm finished.</i>

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:11.720
<i>Don't stop! Move!</i>

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.220
<i>Move! There's no time!</i>

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.470
<i>This is it.</i>

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.690
<i>I was being too cocky.</i>

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:26.570
<i>Why did I think... a half-hearted
sumo wrestler who quit the sport...</i>

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:29.320
<i>could win anything at this level?</i>

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:30.820
Kirihito!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.650
You've got more to give than that!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.290
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.430
<i>I've left myself wide open!</i>

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.780
<i>Finally... you've decided to move.</i>

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.340
<i>I want to help the team, too.</i>

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.800
<i>For just one day in my life...</i>

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.070
<i>For this one bout...</i>

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:07.570
<i>I'm going to push past...</i>

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.530
<i>my limits!</i>

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.910
<i>Basic form: Three-point throw!</i>

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.040
<b>Basic
Form</b>

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.040
<b>Three-Point Throw</b>

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:13.410
<b>Basic
Form</b>

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:13.410
<b>Three-Point Throw</b>

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.160
<b>Basic
Form</b>

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.160
<b>Three-Point Throw</b>

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.910
Go!

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.050
He did it!

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:34.720
No...

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.310
A protest?

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.530
The opponent's strength let him stay in it!

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.100
Hey, now...

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.950
The professor's got nothing left.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:48.130
Don't make him do a do-over.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.660
Hey, are you okay?

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.290
I-I'm fine.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:58.450
Simultaneous landings! Restart the bout!

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.360
No...

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.550
Great...

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.470
Restarting the bout...

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:19.220
Hey...

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.310
Are you okay?

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:24.510
He can't do it! He'll have to forfeit!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:27.000
That's for the professor to decide.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:31.890
But after what Hotaru did in his bout,
I can't see him backing out.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.900
No, that's got nothing to do with it.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.260
<i>That wasn't enough to satisfy you.</i>

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.990
<i>You haven't showcased
your style of sumo yet.</i>

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.640
<i>Your body's just getting warmed up.</i>

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:52.880
<i>I've been given another chance
to contest a sumo bout...</i>

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:54.590
<i>I'm grateful.</i>

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.240
<i>I'm ready to burst.</i>

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.330
He's smiling?

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:05.260
<i>He can't seem to get his
breathing under control.</i>

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:09.900
<i>Just like our captain said,
he's got zero stamina.</i>

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:14.250
<i>If I can grab him and
draw out the bout, I'll win!</i>

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.390
Does he stand any chance of winning?

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:22.040
In his current state, the prof only has
another five seconds in him at most.

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.940
If the opponent wastes time like before...

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:30.200
<i>Our bodies leave us at a disadvantage,
so we rely on our techniques and spirit.</i>

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:31.960
<i>Show them that.</i>

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.490
<i>What is this?</i>

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:40.140
<i>Is this guy really here or not?
His aura's like a ghost's!</i>

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.560
Spirit!

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.640
<i>That was a weak charge!</i>

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:53.150
<b>Head Twist</b>

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.950
<i>Head Twist: Spiral Cut!</i>

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:51.520
<b>Spiral</b>

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:51.900
<b>Spiral</b>

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:52.020
<b>Cut</b>

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.150
<b>Spiral</b>

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:52.400
<b>Cut</b>

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:53.150
<b>Cut</b>

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.300
<i>Yes... This is it...</i>

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:07.790
<i>There's no better feeling.</i>

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:10.890
Wow.

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:15.810
<i>Tsuji-kun, on the east side,
wins with a head twist.</i>

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.090
Good work.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.780
Look at what... you made me do.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.600
If you lose after that, I'm coming after you.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:30.730
Gotcha.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.990
Hey, who told you losing was an option?

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.340
After I gave us a head-start and all...

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.390
Yeah.

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:42.830
You aren't hurt, are you, Leon-chan?

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.970
That was some great sumo.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.210
<i>Our team's as inconsistent as always.</i>

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.180
<i>Thanks, Mitsuhashi!</i>

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:02.850
Two grade schoolers once
set Chiba alight with their sumo.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.130
The hard Onimaru Kunitsuna,
and the soft Onikiri Yasutsuna.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:07.850
I see.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.360
I'd heard he'd quit for a while,

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.110
but looks like he couldn't stay away
from the fun fest that is sumo wrestling.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.100
Wh-What's Hakuro doing here?

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.820
All the good seats were taken.
Sorry for invading your space.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.390
I-Is your leg okay?

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.830
I'm really sorry.

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:29.550
N-N-N-No, I'm sorry as well!

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:30.740
Really sorry!

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.730
Hey, Gojo!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:39.300
I can still see where your 
little sister slapped you!

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.380
<i>That one sure resonated with me.</i>

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:44.800
<i>I'm all good now.</i>

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.700
<i>I'm going to win this one for the team.</i>

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:49.320
Yuma!

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:51.950
Do you love sumo?

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:55.820
This is your last bout.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:58.900
Go do this for yourself.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:02.390
<i>Third bout.</i>

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.940
<i>On the east side, Gojo-kun.</i>

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.810
<i>On the west side, Yomoda-kun.</i>

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:11.270
Yomoda, huh?

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:12.890
He's a dangerous opponent.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.540
Yeah.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:18.990
He hasn't stood on the winners' podium
before, so he doesn't have a moniker,

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:21.800
but he always places highly
in individual tournaments.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.050
You said it.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:26.840
But he held back against me when
I faced him in the third-place bout!

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:28.810
I was looking forward to that!

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.530
<i>Two national treasures are
heaping praise on him...</i>

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:37.530
<i>He's a talented sumo wrestler
in peak condition,</i>

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:41.230
<i>while Yuma's still recovering 
from his semifinal bout.</i>

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:43.030
<i>And Yuma's giving away around 70 kilos.</i>

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.910
<i>How can he win this?</i>

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:47.910
<i>Yuma?</i>

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.360
<i>Gojo, huh?</i>

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:53.790
<i>Considering it's Dachi High we're facing,
it could've been worse,</i>

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:57.560
<i>but I need to watch out for his strikes.</i>

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.050
<i>Then again, if I get in
close and try to grab him,</i>

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.210
<i>I might fall into a trap he's laid
for me, like Batbayar did.</i>

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:06.720
<i>He's sure to start off with palm strikes.</i>

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:11.180
<i>I'll let him hit me and use my 
weight advantage to force him back!</i>

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:12.100
Spirit!

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.160
<i>Remember...</i>

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.360
<i>Outside of Dachi High...</i>

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.860
<i>I wanted to use this sport I love</i>

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.240
<i>to make something of myself!</i>

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:28.740
A lunge punch!

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.200
A solid hit!

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:34.290
You two might not know this, but...

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.940
His strikes really hurt.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.150
Isn't he supposed to be running low on gas?

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.710
What a barrage...

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.600
Yomoda's body is leaning back!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:46.930
Keep it up, Gojo!

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.390
<i>Damn, this guy...</i>

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:53.230
<i>He always seemed to be
at the end of his rope,</i>

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.390
<i>but on this big stage,
he's enjoying himself!</i>

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.650
Keep it up, Yuma!

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.650
Go!

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:00.650
<i>You deserve credit for
seeking redemption.</i>

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.770
<i>But that's not the only reason
you're here, is it?</i>

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:07.400
<i>What your teammates want you
to do the most...</i>

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.000
<i>Yes.</i>

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.200
<i>They want you to engross yourself in sumo!</i>

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.160
Yuma-san!

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:16.660
You've got no room
behind you! Go sideways!

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.370
Use more of the ring!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:21.670
<i>Pulling techniques used
to catch Gojo-san out...</i>

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:23.890
<i>But that was then, and this is now!</i>

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.190
<i>Staying at this distance is dangerous.</i>

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.430
<i>I have to grab his belt!</i>

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:34.600
Yomoda can't do a thing against him.

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:41.560
<i>Partial Lunge: Castle Break Punch!</i>

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:43.920
Yes!

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:46.490
That sly fox.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:54.410
He put distance between them to draw
an expansive strike out of him.

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.000
<i>I've finally got you.</i>

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.380
<i>You think grabbing me ends it?</i>

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.590
<i>Not a chance.</i>

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:08.670
<i>Whose throws do you think
I have to deal with every day?!</i>

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.710
<i>I can feel his full weight when I grab him.</i>

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:19.500
<i>But I've got to finish this!</i>

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:21.610
Break!

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:25.770
Stay exactly where you are.

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:31.290
He's bleeding a lot.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:32.930
A timeout to stop the bleeding.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:37.090
It's good that he gets a chance to rest.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:39.670
Sorry. Are you okay?

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.790
Oh no. It's fine, really.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:47.450
You're pretty strong, aren't you?

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:12.530
<i>Most of the time,</i>

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.530
<i>he's got more than a few screws loose.</i>

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:18.760
<i>But when he puts on his mawashi belt,</i>

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:20.940
<i>the training area takes on a different feel.</i>

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.940
<i>Having him behind me puts me on edge.</i>

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:29.850
<i>I guess he's impatient for 
his bout against Onimaru.</i>

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:34.560
<i>Or maybe it's his awkward way 
of offering encouragement.</i>

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:37.790
Yuma!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.650
Focus.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:42.330
Right.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:45.810
<i>I'm strong, huh?</i>

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.300
<i>No, you're wrong.</i>

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.650
<i>I </i>became<i> strong.</i>

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.700
<i>The Dachi High sumo club
has made me who I am.</i>

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:57.490
<i>I can't put this feeling into words.</i>

00:16:58.820 --> 00:16:59.560
<i>So...</i>

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:04.790
Spirit!

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:09.290
<i>I'll win and make my gratitude tangible!</i>

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.680
<i>The tissues make it hard to breathe,</i>

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:15.800
<i>so I need to finish this now!</i>

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:21.390
<i>I can't overpower him, but...</i>

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:23.390
<i>Ozeki taught me a technique that'll help.</i>

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.100
<i>If I lift up my opponent's right arm,
it raises his center of gravity!</i>

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.300
<i>As long as my center of gravity
 is lower than his...</i>

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:30.770
<i>I can push him!</i>

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.890
<i>This is my last high school sumo bout...</i>

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:39.410
<i>No, my last sumo bout ever!</i>

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.090
Yomo!

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:41.120
Stand strong!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:41.680
Yes!

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:42.330
Go!

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.000
<i>I'll put everything on the line
right here, right now!</i>

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:50.990
Overarm to underarm?

00:17:50.990 --> 00:17:51.710
So fast!

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:54.590
This is what I'm talking about.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:59.090
Looks like I really need to beef up.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.970
<i>He's not lifting with his arms.</i>

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.430
<i>It's all belly.</i>

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:12.400
<i>That's the traditional sumo way.</i>

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:14.940
<i>A team without a star wrestler...</i>

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.030
<i>An off-year...</i>

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.720
<i>A lot of people have disparaged us,</i>

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.090
<i>but now, we have </i>him<i>.</i>

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:25.250
<i>That's why I've staked it all
on the team tournament!</i>

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:29.210
<i>Winning here is what a captain does!</i>

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:31.840
Wriggle yourself free, Yuma!

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:41.510
Wriggle more! Like your life depends on it!

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:43.140
<i>Strong...</i>

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:46.000
<i>He's strong and...</i>

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.080
<i>I want to beat him!</i>

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.320
<i>Just like back then...</i>

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:00.100
<i>I want to set myself ablaze again!</i>

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.040
<i>You've only been doing sumo for a few months.</i>

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:13.680
<i>If you ask me,
you're a prodigious talent yourself.</i>

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:23.840
<i>Yomoda-kun, on the west side,
wins by push down.</i>

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:27.720
<i>If I hadn't saved my
strength coming into this,</i>

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:29.690
<i>I would've been in real trouble.</i>

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.300
Yuma...

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.450
Yuma-san...

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:49.560
He's become... a real sumo wrestler.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:50.960
Yeah.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:57.910
Dammit!

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:00.370
How was it?

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:03.990
Sumo's fun, isn't it?

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:06.640
I didn't really have time to enjoy it.

00:20:08.590 --> 00:20:10.010
But, you know...

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.210
It <i>was</i> fun!

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:17.850
<i>So that was my last bout, huh?</i>

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:21.550
<i>Wish I could have gone out with a bang.</i>

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:30.650
<i>I'm not sure I can quit sumo after that.</i>

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:33.510
That's Odachi's second loss.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:35.290
They're teetering on the edge.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:39.460
You wouldn't know it by 
looking at them, though.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:43.700
There's no telling who's 
gonna win this match.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:19.190
<b>Odachi
High
School
Sumo
Club</b>

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:22.690
Women are forbidden from entering
the sumo ring, so I am a little nervous.

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:24.920
That only applies to pro bouts.

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:27.450
Plenty of girls do sumo
at the amateur level.

00:22:27.730 --> 00:22:31.700
I guess this will improve our understanding
of sumo and make us better managers.

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:34.700
Okay, here I come.

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:36.150
Spirit!

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:51.340
<b>Odachi
High
School
Sumo
Club</b>

00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:57.250
<i>Hori-chan is more knowledgeable...</i>

00:22:57.250 --> 00:22:59.600
<i>but I'm way more athletic!</i>

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:01.790
<i>Th-This is rather fun!</i>

00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.280
H-Hey, wait!

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:07.300
You're wide open!

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:16.660
<b>Winning Technique</b>

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:16.660
<b>Partial Throw</b>

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:16.660
<b>Winner</b>

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:16.660
<b>Reina</b>

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Winning Technique</b>

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Partial Throw</b>

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Winner</b>

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:17.290
<b>Reina</b>

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.410
<b>Winning Technique</b>

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.410
<b>Partial Throw</b>

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.410
<b>Winner</b>

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:18.410
<b>Reina</b>

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:22.430
I'm sure I don't need to tell you what'll
happen if you breathe a word of this.

00:23:22.430 --> 00:23:23.270
Yes, ma'am.

00:23:23.270 --> 00:23:24.650
But, you know...

00:23:24.650 --> 00:23:28.720
Hori-chan will go around
telling everyone you peeked up her skirt!

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:30.930
<b>Next Bout    "Spirit"</b>

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:30.170
<i>Me</i>?!
